    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350-a3">

                <pb facs="0465" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg357"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 129.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mevs to Mr.
                            Terres.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-11-18T15:00:00-04:49"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                                1892</hi>, 3 o’clock p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith beg to advise you that I am
                    still retained in prison without a hearing, which, according to Haitian law,
                    should have taken place within forty-eight hours of my arrest, in default of
                    which it becomes amenable to damages.</p>
                <p>I formally protest against this arbitrary manner of treating an American citizen
                    by the Haitian authorities in direct violation of their own laws.</p>
                <p>Trusting that you have and are still giving my case your careful attention,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederick Mevs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
